      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Buyer Setup Guide\n\nConfigure these n8n environment variables:\n- `OPENAI_API_KEY` — OpenAI credential/API setup for the AI model nodes\n- `FEEDBACK_SHEET_ID` — destination Google Sheet ID\n- `FEEDBACK_SHEET_NAME` — destination sheet/tab name\n- `SUPPORT_ESCALATION_EMAIL` — urgent-feedback inbox\n- `BRAND_NAME` — customer-facing business name\n- `SUPPORT_AGENT_NAME` — support representative name\n\nRequired Google Sheet columns:\n`Customer`, `Customer Email`, `Order ID`, `Feedback`, `Sentiment`, `Category`, `Summary`, `Urgent`, `Escalated To`, `Date`\n\nConnect the buyer's own OpenAI and Google Sheets credentials in n8n.\n\nTest positive, neutral, and urgent feedback before enabling production automation."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f8cc4a46-783b-432f-a388-5035366f7a63",
      "name": "NOTES • Automation Safety & Limitations",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2368,
        -2064
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Automation Safety & Limitations\n\n- AI classification is a triage signal, not a guaranteed judgement.\n- Review business-critical or sensitive complaints.\n- Customer emails must not invent refunds, policies, deadlines, causes, or resolutions.\n- Feedback can contain personal information; follow the buyer's privacy and retention policies.\n- Keep escalation routing and support processes maintained.\n- Test every branch before activating the workflow.\n- Workflow is inactive by default.\n- Use buyer-owned credentials and data."
      }
    }
